# BotShieldHeuristicTrigger — a starting slate, not a compiled-in default.
#
# Nothing here is enforced automatically. The module ships no default
# rules: an unset score threshold never fires, so a fresh deployment
# scores nothing and challenges nothing until you declare both a
# heuristic (or trigger) and a threshold. That is deliberate — a
# default every deployment has to disable was not a default, and every
# lockout this module has caused traced back to an implicit weight
# nobody had written down. This file is what the module used to seed
# automatically, kept as a documented starting point for anyone who
# wants that shape rather than building it from a blank slate. It is
# NOT a required include, and it does nothing until you paste some or
# all of it into your own config. tests/setup/botshield-dev.conf carries the
# same slate wired into a live vhost, if you want to see it running
# rather than read about it.
#
# Heuristics are the cheap built-in score signals — UA / header
# patterns and first-sight Bloom-filter checks — that fire before any
# operator-configured trigger or rate-limit rule. Promoting them to a
# directive family means an operator can tune individual penalties,
# disable a single heuristic, or wipe the whole slate and build it back
# up from zero, all without recompiling the module.
#
# Syntax:
#   BotShieldHeuristicTrigger <name>|all [reset] [action=<verb> args...]
#
# Names:
#   missingua       UA header absent or empty.
#   missingal       Accept-Language header absent or empty.
#   scraperua       UA contains a known HTTP-library token (curl,
#                    Wget, python-requests, urllib, httpx, aiohttp,
#                    Go-http-client, okhttp, axios, scrapy, java,
#                    libwww, lwp-request, ...).
#   firstsightip   Client IP not seen in the rotating Bloom filter
#                    (cookieless / signature-mismatched requests
#                    only — sig-verified clients skip this signal).
#   droppedcookie   Client IP IS in the Bloom filter (it has been
#                    seen before) but the request carries no cookie
#                    holding solve proof. Gated on solve proof rather
#                    than mere cookie validity — a client that merely
#                    kept an old cookie without ever passing a
#                    challenge does not earn the waiver.
#
# Action verbs (same as BotShieldFlagTrigger):
#   action=score add=N             (signed; SUM across matching entries)
#   action=tier_floor min=<tier>   (pass|noninteractive|interactive|captcha; MAX)
#
# Reset:
#   BotShieldHeuristicTrigger <name> reset           # clear that name
#   BotShieldHeuristicTrigger <name> reset action=...  # clear + redeclare
#   BotShieldHeuristicTrigger all reset              # wipe every entry
#                                                    # this scope declared
#
# Observe-mode (logs `<reason>:observe` instead of applying):
#   BotShieldHeuristicTrigger missingua action=score add=40 mode=observe

# --- The starter slate -------------------------------------------------
# Conservative score adds — none alone is enough to cross a
# noninteractive threshold of 20 (a value you would set yourself; see
# BotShieldScoreNonInteractive in docs/directives.md). Two together (a
# curl with no Accept-Language: 40 + 5 + 20 first-sight = 65) clears an
# interactive threshold of 50. The shape rewards "looks like a real
# browser" and costs "looks like a script." Values match the
# BS_PENALTY_* constants in src/score.h at the time this file was
# written; the module never reads this file, so it cannot drift from
# those constants on its own — if you copy these lines, they are yours
# to keep in sync.
<BotShieldHeuristicTrigger missingua>
    BotShieldAction       score
    BotShieldAdd          40
</BotShieldHeuristicTrigger>
<BotShieldHeuristicTrigger missingal>
    BotShieldAction       score
    BotShieldAdd          5
</BotShieldHeuristicTrigger>
<BotShieldHeuristicTrigger scraperua>
    BotShieldAction       score
    BotShieldAdd          10
</BotShieldHeuristicTrigger>
<BotShieldHeuristicTrigger firstsightip>
    BotShieldAction       score
    BotShieldAdd          20
</BotShieldHeuristicTrigger>
<BotShieldHeuristicTrigger droppedcookie>
    BotShieldAction       score
    BotShieldAdd          25
</BotShieldHeuristicTrigger>

# --- Common overrides ------------------------------------------------
#
# Soften the missing-UA penalty (keep it as a signal but don't bump
# tier on its own):
#   BotShieldHeuristicTrigger missingua reset action=score add=10
#
# Disable scraper-UA matching entirely (e.g., when a legitimate API
# integration uses a Go-http-client UA):
#   BotShieldHeuristicTrigger scraperua reset
#
# Promote firstsightip from a small score nudge to a tier_floor.
# Every never-before-seen client lands in the noninteractive tier
# regardless of their other signals; a verified pass graduates them out:
#   BotShieldHeuristicTrigger firstsightip reset
#   BotShieldHeuristicTrigger firstsightip action=tier_floor min=noninteractive
#
# Stage a tighter scraper-UA penalty in observe mode for one release
# before enforcing:
#   BotShieldHeuristicTrigger scraperua action=score add=80 mode=observe
#   # logs `scraperua-<token>:observe` on every fire; drop
#   # mode=observe once the rate looks right.
#
# Multiple actions on the same heuristic accumulate (SUM for score,
# MAX for tier_floor). Example: keep the +10 score above AND add a
# tier_floor for an extra-strict deployment:
#   BotShieldHeuristicTrigger scraperua action=tier_floor min=interactive
#   # combined effect: +10 score AND a tier floor at interactive
